<section class="section page-header" data-screen-label="Page header"> <div class="section-inner"> <span class="eyebrow reveal">About · STS</span> <h1 class="page-title reveal">If corruption was built intentionally, <span class="accent">integrity must be built intentionally</span>.</h1> <p class="page-lede reveal">Street-To-Stardom is the education, mentorship and youth-development arm of Afrovanguard. Four programs across four Lagos LGAs, with cohorts capped at 24 and outcomes published every term.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section prose-section" data-screen-label="About · Origin"> <div class="section-inner"> <div class="prose-grid"> <div> <div class="meta">01 · Origin</div> <div style="margin-top: 16px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 240px;">
Founded 2021 · An Afrovanguard initiative · Operating in Alimosho, Ikeja, Kosofe and Agege LGAs.
</div> </div> <div class="prose"> <p>Street-To-Stardom was founded from a deep dissatisfaction with the growing culture of corruption, indiscipline, hopelessness and misdirection among children, teenagers and adults across society.</p> <p>The vision emerged from a painful realisation: that society often tries to fix corruption at the top while neglecting the roots — childhood, broken value systems, poor mentorship, cultural disconnection, and the absence of intentional leadership development. Rather than criticise the system from a distance, STS was created as a practical grassroots antidote — a transformational movement designed to rebuild character, leadership, creativity, discipline, competence and responsibility from the foundation upward.</p> <blockquote>
If corruption was built intentionally, integrity must also be built intentionally.
<cite>— Founding statement, 2021</cite> </blockquote> <h3>How it began</h3> <p>The initiative was inspired and championed by <strong>Ogunbanjo Anuoluwapo Oluwaseun</strong>, a member of the Afrovanguard Board of Trustees, whose passion for children, education, leadership and community advancement led to the development of several grassroots transformation programs that later evolved into the STS movement.</p> <p>The foundation of STS was built through the integration of four community-focused initiatives:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Next Generation Genius Club</strong> — weekend STEM + creative-thinking labs for ages 9–14</li> <li><strong>Alimosho Summer School</strong> — a six-week intensive bridging the long-vacation learning gap</li> <li><strong>LCASP</strong> — the Lagos Community Advancement School Project, our flagship literacy and numeracy intervention</li> <li><strong>STREET Storm</strong> — out-of-school youth mentorship and vocational onboarding</li> </ul> <p>These programs were originally designed to mentor children and teenagers, provide educational support, expose young people to leadership and creativity, build discipline and self-worth, reconnect youths to purpose, and create a healthier future for African communities.</p> <p>Over time it became clear that these were not isolated programs — they were parts of a larger vision: a unified grassroots transformation ecosystem capable of raising a generation that is intellectually sound, morally disciplined, culturally grounded, technologically empowered and socially responsible. That ecosystem became Street-To-Stardom.</p> <h3>What we are, plainly</h3> <p>Four programs. One framework. A small staff, a governing council, and a growing volunteer corps. We do not run a school. We run with schools, around schools, after school. Cohort sizes are deliberately small. Reporting is deliberately granular.</p> <h3>What we are not</h3> <p>We are not a charity in the giving-tin sense. Every shilling we receive is reported against a published cost ledger; the ratio of programmatic to overhead spend appears in our annual report and again in the audited financials. We are not a research institute, but we run our programs with a research-institute's appetite for measurement.</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section" data-screen-label="About · Vision &amp; Mission" style="padding-top: 32px; padding-bottom: 96px;"> <div class="section-inner"> <span class="eyebrow reveal">Vision &amp; mission</span> <h2 class="section-title reveal" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 36px); margin-bottom: 40px;">Two sentences. The work behind each.</h2> <div class="duo-cards"> <div class="duo-card blue reveal"> <span class="duo-label">Vision · 2030</span> <h3>A Lagos in which every child has documented access to a literate, character-rich education by the end of primary school.</h3> <p>"Documented" is the operative word. We don't aim to be the largest provider. We aim to be the most transparent — and to push everyone else in our field toward the same standard.</p> </div> <div class="duo-card crimson reveal"> <span class="duo-label">Mission · today</span> <h3>Run small, measurable, replicable programs that close documented learning gaps and rebuild integrity from the grassroots up.</h3> <p>Cohorts of 24 maximum. Baseline-endline data on every child. Methodology and findings published openly, including the parts that didn't work.</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section" data-screen-label="About · Pillars" style="padding-top:8px;padding-bottom:72px;"> <div class="section-inner"> <span class="eyebrow reveal">How transformation happens</span> <h2 class="section-title reveal" style="font-size:clamp(28px,3.4vw,36px);">Five pillars, cultivated every programme day.</h2> <p class="section-lede reveal">Whatever the programme, the work shapes a child across the same five dimensions — the heart of the STS Transformation Cycle.</p> <div class="sts-pillars" style="margin-top:36px;"> <div class="sts-pill-card reveal"><div class="n">Pillar 01</div><div class="t">Character</div><div class="d">Integrity, discipline and ethical decision-making — practised, not just preached.</div></div> <div class="sts-pill-card reveal"><div class="n">Pillar 02</div><div class="t">Leadership</div><div class="d">Influence through service, modelled for schools, communities and nations.</div></div> <div class="sts-pill-card reveal"><div class="n">Pillar 03</div><div class="t">Skill</div><div class="d">Future-ready competencies: AI, coding, entrepreneurship, media and the arts.</div></div> <div class="sts-pill-card reveal"><div class="n">Pillar 04</div><div class="t">Community</div><div class="d">Civic responsibility through volunteerism and real service-learning.</div></div> <div class="sts-pill-card reveal"><div class="n">Pillar 05</div><div class="t">Purpose</div><div class="d">Identity, destiny and a child's responsibility toward Africa and humanity.</div></div> </div> <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:26px;"> <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/methodology">See the full Transformation Cycle <span class="btn-arrow">→</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section class="sts-photoband" data-screen-label="About · In the field" style="padding-bottom:88px;"> <div class="sts-photoband__grid"> <figure class="sts-figure sts-figure--tall reveal"><img loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/summer2.png" alt="Children at Alimosho Summer School"/><figcaption>Alimosho Summer School</figcaption></figure> <figure class="sts-figure reveal"><img loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/storm1.png" alt="Street Storm community outreach"/><figcaption>Street Storm · outreach</figcaption></figure> <figure class="sts-figure reveal"><img loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/bootcamp1.png" alt="Next Generation Genius bootcamp"/><figcaption>NextGen Genius · bootcamp</figcaption></figure> <figure class="sts-figure reveal"><img loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/culture1.png" alt="Creative arts and culture session"/><figcaption>Creative arts &amp; culture</figcaption></figure> <figure class="sts-figure reveal"><img loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/summer5.png" alt="Learning session in progress"/><figcaption>Learning in progress</figcaption></figure> </div> </section> <section class="section" data-screen-label="About · Afrovanguard" style="padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 96px; background: var(--surface); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);"> <div class="section-inner"> <div class="prose-grid"> <div> <div class="meta">02 · Parent brand</div> <div class="reveal" style="margin-top: 16px;"> <img alt="STS" height="48" src="/assets/sts-logo.svg" width="48"/> <div style="margin-top: 12px; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.04em;">STS</div> <div style="margin-top: 24px; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--muted);">AFROVANGUARD</div> </div> </div> <div class="prose"> <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Our relationship with Afrovanguard</h3> <p>Street-To-Stardom operates under the institutional framework of <strong>Afrovanguard</strong> as one of its flagship transformational projects — focused on rebuilding Africa from the grassroots through mentorship, education, technology, creativity, leadership development, culture, community engagement and strategic partnerships. Afrovanguard provides the institutional scaffolding; STS does the program work.</p> <p>In practice this means a shared Board of Trustees, a shared safeguarding policy, and a single audited set of financial statements that breaks out our share of the budget line by line. The two brands are kept visually distinct so that supporters always know who is doing what.</p> <p><a href="https://afrovanguard.org.ng" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Visit Afrovanguard <span style="display: inline-block; margin-left: 4px;">↗</span></a></p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section" data-screen-label="About · Leadership preview" style="padding-top: 96px; padding-bottom: 96px;"> <div class="section-inner"> <div class="what-head"> <div> <span class="eyebrow reveal">Leadership</span> <h2 class="section-title reveal">A small team of practitioners. A council that holds them to it.</h2> </div> <div class="reveal"> <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/team">See the full team <span class="btn-arrow">→</span></a> </div> </div> <div class="people-grid"> <div class="person reveal"> <div class="placeholder" style=""><img alt="Ogunbanjo – programme team" loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/anuoluwapo-ogunbanjo.jpg" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;z-index:2;"/></div> <div class="person-name">Ogunbanjo Anuoluwapo Oluwaseun</div> <div class="person-role">Founder · STS · BOT, Afrovanguard</div> <div class="person-bio">Inspired and championed the STS movement. Trustee at Afrovanguard whose work in education, leadership and grassroots community development became the foundation of the four-stream STS ecosystem.</div> </div><div class="person reveal"> <div class="placeholder" style=""><img alt="Chinwe – programme team" loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/tayo-adeyemo.jpg" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;z-index:2;"/></div> <div class="person-name">Chinwe Adeyemi</div> <div class="person-role">Head of Research</div> <div class="person-bio">Education researcher (UI, MEd). Owns baseline-endline methodology and the public data releases.</div> </div><div class="person reveal"> <div class="placeholder" style=""><img alt="Mariam – programme team" loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/anuoluwapo-ogunbanjo.jpg" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;z-index:2;"/></div> <div class="person-name">Mariam Olatunji</div> <div class="person-role">Director, LCASP</div> <div class="person-bio">School-relations lead. Sits in the partner schools more days than she sits in our office.</div> </div><div class="person reveal"> <div class="placeholder" style=""><img alt="Femi – programme team" loading="lazy" src="https://afrovanguard.org.ng/Images/tayo-adeyemo.jpg" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;z-index:2;"/></div> <div class="person-name">Femi Ojo</div> <div class="person-role">Director, NextGen</div> <div class="person-bio">Designer-turned-educator. Built the year-long Genius Club curriculum from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section cta-strip" data-screen-label="Page CTA"> <div class="section-inner"> <div class="cta-strip-inner reveal"> <div> <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">Next · See the programs</div> <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 36px); max-width: 600px;">The four programs we run, with methodology and results.</h2> </div> <div class="cta-strip-actions"> <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/programs">Explore programs <span class="btn-arrow">→</span></a> <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/impact">Read the evidence</a> </div> </div> </div> </section>
